This directory contains sample ".motifbind" files:

CDE - Common Desktop Environment bindings for a generic keyboard, with
      Ctrl+C, Ctrl+X and Ctrl+V for copy, cut and paste
pc  - OSF/Motif Style Guide bindings for PC keyboards

They are installed in share/X11/bindings.  Motif does not read them on
its own.  To use one, copy it to ~/.motifbind, where mwm, xmbind and
Motif applications look for it, or load it into the running X server
with

    xmbind /usr/share/X11/bindings/CDE

Without ~/.motifbind and without a bindings property on the root window,
Motif uses its built-in bindings.  See VirtualBindings(3) and xmbind(1).

Earlier releases also shipped bindings for old vendor workstations
(DEC, HaL, HP, IBM, SGI, Sony, Sun) and an xmbind.alias file that chose
one of them from the X server vendor string.  Current X servers report
vendor strings that none of those entries matched, so the files and the
alias lookup were removed.  The bindings for those vendors that libXm
has always carried built in are still chosen by vendor string.
